{"kind":"request","text":"Security R9, R10 and R11 (6dd06d03 sections 3 and 5): settings and trust.\n\nWork:\n1. R9. One parser for each setting, shared by every reader: ARTIFACTS_CONFIG, the GitHub settings, DEPLOYMENT and APPLICATION_TRUST. The site route uses the same Artifacts parser as the wiring (3.5).\n2. R9. /health reports the wiring state, not only registerScope: Artifacts wired, NO_OUTSIDE or ambiguous; GitHub wired, or off with its reason. A configured wiring that is off answers 503 (3.5).\n3. R9. One DEPLOYMENT bound, 1 to 128 bytes, in sessions, demo creation, health, metrics and screens (3.6).\n4. R9. `npm run deploy:scope` keeps settings set outside the file (--keep-vars), or a plan check refuses a deploy that drops a setting (3.10).\n5. R10. MCP `install_application` checks the release against APPLICATION_TRUST before any fetch. A trust row carries the host, and the fetch goes only to that host (3.7).\n6. R11. When a release leaves APPLICATION_TRUST, acts under its definitions are refused with a named reason, or the revocation is recorded as an act. State the choice in the head (3.8).\n\nWitnesses: one for each item, including a namespace mismatch and a malformed optional GitHub secret that now show in /health with 503, a 129-byte DEPLOYMENT refused everywhere, an untrusted install refused with no outbound fetch, and an act under a revoked release refused.\n\nThe planner's dap-grow deploy passes three settings by --var. The head's report gives the deploy command after this change. Closes 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, 3.8 and 3.10.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 6 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Shared setting parsers, wiring-state health, one DEPLOYMENT bound, keep-vars or plan check, install_application trust-before-fetch with host, revoked releases refuse; closes 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, 3.8, 3.10. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}